{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793921261,"nonce":"GteRnlF1GD+atGhUoTzH+tmrsIM=","title":"git work pull, push and sync fail on a URL instead of a remote name","message":"Found while doing e66709b. `git work pull \u003cURL\u003e` fails at the fetch: `gitcli.FetchRefs` builds `refs/\u003cns\u003e/*:refs/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/\u003cns\u003e/*`, so a URL ends up inside a ref name and git rejects the refspec. MergeAll then reads `refs/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/...` the same way. Check whether push and sync fail similarly, along with the go-git paths (`resolveRemote`, the in-memory fetch refspec in `PushRefs`).\n\n**Expected.** Either a URL works, or the command refuses it up front with a clear error naming the fix (`git remote add NAME URL`), instead of a raw refspec error from git.\n\n**Default decision (2026-11-05): refuse, unless supporting URLs turns out to be trivial.** Remote-tracking refs and merge state are keyed by a remote's name, and the model is one team, one repository, one remote. Inventing a name for a URL would leave orphaned `refs/remotes/\u003cmangled\u003e/` trees behind. `git work install` already refuses an unconfigured remote (`gitcli.ErrRemoteNotConfigured`); pull, push and sync should refuse in the same way and give the same advice.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["core"],"parent":"bc14d4d88d377f01d8cdafffc35fa0ee11b5b4795ec8034742de3e1cc15858ac","priority":"low","status":"in-progress","type":"task"}}]}